# UI and UX

## Foundation

- Use existing shadcn components under [src/components/ui](src/components/ui) and [components.json](components.json) (`radix-lyra`, `mist`, Lucide, CSS variables in [src/app/globals.css](src/app/globals.css)).
- Inspect local components before adding new ones; do not duplicate primitives that already exist.
- Do not build a parallel design system on `@radix-ui/themes` unless the task is explicitly about that package (layout currently imports Themes CSS only).
- Physician public pages use the same design system with limited, validated settings (navigation, sections, service cards, contact). That is not a page builder and must not accept arbitrary HTML or scripts.

## Quality bar

- Semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, visible focus, labels, and clear validation feedback.
- Responsive layouts (mobile, tablet, desktop).
- Loading, empty, error, success, and destructive-action states for administrative and clinical flows.
- Forms must stay usable with long descriptions and validation text.
- Clinical and financial screens follow [persian-rtl.mdc](.cursor/rules/persian-rtl.mdc): natural Persian, logical CSS, and readable mixed-direction text (names, abbreviations, phone numbers, amounts).

## Avoid generic AI UI

No unmotivated gradients, glow, glassmorphism, decorative backgrounds, excessive nested cards/shadows, emoji as icons, decorative motion, fake stats, invented patients, invented services, invented reviews, or arbitrary typography/color.

[src/components/ui/auth-card.tsx](src/components/ui/auth-card.tsx) uses gradient and motion. Leave it until a dedicated UI task. Do not copy that treatment onto clinical, financial, or physician-site screens.

The home page in [src/app/page.tsx](src/app/page.tsx) still uses store wording. Do not treat that copy as the product direction. Follow shadcn tokens and existing `Button` patterns.

## Persian RTL

All UI must follow [persian-rtl.mdc](.cursor/rules/persian-rtl.mdc) (mandatory, always on). [components.json](components.json) `"rtl": true` supports the kit; application copy and document `lang`/`dir` are defined there, not here.
